termination, the Qwen cross-scale analysis, and the arXiv null result into distinct sections rather than grouping them under broader claims. I'm laying out the full paper structure with sections for each major experiment—the K* characterization work, the curation results including the null finding from arXiv, and the robustness validation studies. Now I need to decide on a document class and template for writing this up, though I'll start with a basic article format since I don't have access to the ACL style files.\n\nLet me draft the complete paper now, making sure to incorporate all the experimental data, follow the narrative framing, and maintain proper academic writing conventions throughout.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7045,"cache_read_input_tokens":32291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7045},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77007605-4c46-46a1-9837-c424a2ae6462","uuid":"ae40f935-a3f0-4eb7-8bc8-8cc0fa4acba4"}
